NAME
       likeos-install.conf - answers for an unattended LikeOS installation

SYNOPSIS
       likeos-install --answers file

DESCRIPTION
       An  answer file holds everything likeos-install(1) would otherwise ask:
       the disk to install on, the language, the time zone, the keyboard,  the
       computer's  name,  the  root  password and the account to sign in with.
       Given with --answers, it makes the installation unattended.

       The file is UTF-8 text with one setting per line,

              key=value

       Blanks around the key and the value are ignored.  Empty lines and lines
       starting with # are ignored.  A value may be put in double quotes;  in-
       side  them  \"  stands for a quote, \\ for a backslash and \n for a new
       line, and blanks and # are kept.  After the closing quote  only  blanks
       and  a comment may follow.  An unknown key, a bad value or a line with-
       out = stops the installation before anything is changed, with the  file
       name and line number.

       Every key may be left out; the default is given below.

KEYS
   The disk
       disk=device|auto
              The  disk  to  install  on: /dev/sda, sda or /dev/nvme0n1.  auto
              (the default) takes the only disk LikeOS can  be  installed  on,
              and  is  refused  when there is more than one.  The disk the in-
              staller was started from cannot be chosen.

       whole_disk=yes|no
              yes (the default) erases the whole disk: a  new  GUID  partition
              table, an EFI system partition of 512 MiB (FAT32) and the LikeOS
              root  file system (ext4) in the rest.  no installs on one parti-
              tion of the disk, given with root_partition;  the  other  parti-
              tions are kept.

       root_partition=n
              With  whole_disk=no: the number of the partition LikeOS goes to.
              It is formatted with ext4 (everything on it is lost) and must be
              large enough for the system.  The disk must have an  EFI  system
              partition  (FAT, at least 100 MB) apart from it; the boot loader
              is put there next to what it holds already.

       reboot=yes|no
              Restart the computer into the installed system  when  done  (de-
              fault yes).

   Language and region
       locale=locale
              The  language of the installed system, as a locale name (default
              en_US.UTF-8).

       time_format=locale
              How dates, times and numbers are shown (default en_US.UTF-8).

       timezone=zone
              The time zone,  as  a  name  of  the  time  zone  database:  Eu-
              rope/Berlin, America/New_York, UTC (the default).

   Keyboard
       keyboard=layout[,layout...]
              The  keyboard  layouts,  up to four, separated by commas, as XKB
              layout names: us, de, fr, gb ... (default us).  With  more  than
              one, Alt+Shift switches between them.

       keyboard_variant=variant[,variant...]
              The  variant of each layout, in the same order, an empty one for
              the layout's own: nodeadkeys, for keyboard=de,us.   When  given,
              there must be as many as there are layouts.

       keyboard_options=options
              XKB options, separated by commas (grp:alt_shift_toggle, caps:es-
              cape...).

   This computer
       hostname=name
              The  computer's  name:  letters, digits and hyphens, at most 63,
              with at least one letter, not starting or ending with a  hyphen,
              no  dots  (no domain) and not localhost.  The default is likeos-
              followed by four random hexadecimal digits.

       root_password=password
              The password of root, as plain text.

       root_password_hash=hash
              The password of root as a crypt(3) hash ($y$...   yescrypt,  $6$
              ...),  used  when root_password is not given.  One of the two is
              required.

   The account
       The account to  sign  in  with.   It  is  created  when  user_name  (or
       user_fullname) is given, and then needs a password too.

       user_fullname=name
              The full name of the person ("Erika Mustermann").

       user_name=name
              The  user  name:  lower-case letters, digits, hyphens and under-
              scores, starting with a letter or an underscore, at most 32, and
              not the name of a system account.

       user_password=password
              The account's password, as plain text.

       user_password_hash=hash
              The account's password as a crypt(3) hash, used when  user_pass-
              word is not given.

       user_extra_groups=yes|no
              Put  the  account in the groups audio, render and users (default
              yes), so it can play sound and use the graphics hardware.

SECURITY
       An answer file with plain-text passwords gives them to anyone  who  can
       read  it.  Prefer the _hash keys; files the installer saves itself have
       mode 0600 and hold hashes unless asked to keep the plain passwords.

EXAMPLE
       # likeos-install.conf -- answers for an unattended LikeOS installation
       # (likeos-install --answers FILE).  See likeos-install.conf(5).

       disk=/dev/nvme0n1
       whole_disk=yes
       reboot=yes

       # Language, formats, time zone
       locale=de_DE.UTF-8
       time_format=de_DE.UTF-8
       timezone=Europe/Berlin

       # Keyboard
       keyboard=de,us
       keyboard_variant=nodeadkeys,
       keyboard_options=grp:alt_shift_toggle

       # This computer
       hostname=office-pc
       root_password_hash=$y$j9T$...

       # Your account
       user_fullname="Erika Mustermann"
       user_name=erika
       user_password_hash=$y$j9T$...
       user_extra_groups=yes

SEE ALSO
       likeos-install(1), likeos-installer(1), crypt(3), fstab(5)

